
<p>Apple Newsroom’s “Pro and Tell” announcement week continues:</p>

<blockquote>
  <p>Apple today announced the new <a href="https://www.apple.com/macbook-pro/">14-inch MacBook Pro with M6</a>,
delivering even more performance, powerful on-device AI
capabilities, and faster connectivity for college students,
business users, creators, and more. M6 features an advanced
12-core CPU with the world’s fastest CPU core, so everything from
productivity tasks to more demanding pro workflows feels
incredibly fast and responsive. The 12-core GPU delivers up to 30
percent faster graphics and up to 25 percent faster AI workloads
when compared to M5, making the 14-inch MacBook Pro with M6 a
compelling value for users who need serious power. For those
upgrading from M1, the performance gains are even more
significant, with up to 11× faster graphics and up to 13× faster
AI performance. With additional Neural Accelerators in the GPU and
a Dual 16-core Neural Engine, M6 turns MacBook Pro into an even
more powerful platform for AI — from taking advantage of Siri AI
and Apple Intelligence features across apps and macOS to running
LLMs locally, all while preserving user privacy. In addition, the
14-inch MacBook Pro features Wi-Fi 7 and Bluetooth 6, while
superfast storage makes working with large files, exporting
projects, and running demanding AI workflows fly.</p>
</blockquote>

<p>I questioned Apple’s decision to close up “superfast” there, but I stand corrected — <a href="https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/superfast">it is</a>, in fact, a perfectly cromulent adjective. I learn something every day.</p>

<p>Anyway, this is just the base MacBook Pro, the one that’s more like a MacBook Air Plus than a true professional laptop with an M-series Pro or Max chip. This tier of MacBook Pro has only ever been offered in the smaller 14-inch size. Prices seem unchanged from the post-June-price-hike M5 models:</p>

<pre><code>Base price:     $2000

  RAM:  16 GB      +0
        24 GB    +200
        32 GB    +400

  SSD:   1 TB      +0
         2 TB    +500
         4 TB   +1500
</code></pre>

<p>Space black and silver colors, and nano-texture is available for $150 extra.</p>

